-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5685+): Add optional **leaderhead art per era** with the new `EraArtDefineTags` and `EraArtDefineTag` XML fields; e.g., Gandhi's appearance and button changing at Ancient, Classical, Medieval, etc. Currently only a few leaders have such per-era alternative art; the feature is implemented gradually. Note: This is **per-player** not human-centered; e.g. even if the human player is at Medieval Era, if the rival Gandhi is still at Classical Era then Gandhi will use the Classical Era (if set). If none is set or disabled in SAS defines, the art defaults to the base `ArtDefineTag`. Note 2: due to a Civ4 limitation, if a leader (e.g., Gandhi) is used by several players (e.g., in Custom Game), only the first of these leaders' current era is used to select the art for all instances of that leader regardless of their own progress (e.g., if Gandhi 1 is at Medieval and Gandhi 2 and 3 are still at Classical, then Gandhi 2 and 3 will use Gandhi 1's Medieval art). See [README.md (EraArtDefineTags and EraArtDefineTag for leaderhead era art)](/README.md#eraartdefinetags-and-eraartdefinetag-for-leaderhead-era-art) and [KI#120](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#120---documented-known-limitation-per-era-leader-art-shows-the-lowest-index-players-era-when-the-same-leader-is-assigned-to-multiple-players).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5685+): Add optional **leaderhead art per era** with the new `EraArtDefineTags` and `EraArtDefineTag` XML fields; e.g., Gandhi's appearance and button changing at Ancient, Classical, Medieval, etc. Currently only a few leaders have such per-era alternative art; the feature **is technically functional** but leaderhead era **art for each leader is added gradually**. Note: This is **per-player** not human-centered; e.g. even if the human player is at Medieval Era, if the rival Gandhi is still at Classical Era then Gandhi will use the Classical Era (if set). If none is set or disabled in SAS defines, the art defaults to the base `ArtDefineTag`. Note 2: due to a Civ4 limitation, if a leader (e.g., Gandhi) is used by several players (e.g., in Custom Game), only the first of these leaders' current era is used to select the art for all instances of that leader regardless of their own progress (e.g., if Gandhi 1 is at Medieval and Gandhi 2 and 3 are still at Classical, then Gandhi 2 and 3 will use Gandhi 1's Medieval art). See [README.md (EraArtDefineTags and EraArtDefineTag for leaderhead era art)](/README.md#eraartdefinetags-and-eraartdefinetag-for-leaderhead-era-art) and [KI#120](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#120---documented-known-limitation-per-era-leader-art-shows-the-lowest-index-players-era-when-the-same-leader-is-assigned-to-multiple-players).
 - Each leader now has **distinct leader music** (previous BTS/AdvCiv shared tracks split per leader). See [Copyright & disclaimer](/README.md#copyright-and-disclaimer). Note: switched **De Gaulle** from Louis' music in Base AdvCiv to Base Civ4's Napoleon's music, and added an AdvCiv-SAS specific new music for Napoleon so each leader has its own specific music, see [KI#98](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#98---fixed-base-advciv-issue-of-de-gaulle-using-louis-music-instead-of-the-music-common-to-de-gaulle-and-napoleon).
 - **Trait overhaul:** Overhauled for historical fit + gameplay relevance. **Examples:**: Julius Caesar Organized + Imperialist → Aggressive + Imperialist *(military conqueror; offensive pressure)*; Hammurabi Organized + Aggressive → Organized + Protective *(lawgiver/administrator; defensive empire)*; Saladin Protective + Spiritual → Spiritual + Charismatic *(religious leader with battlefield charisma; warmonger in Civ IV terms)*; Isabella Spiritual + Expansive → Spiritual + Aggressive *(zealous, hard-edged campaigns)*; Charlemagne — Imperialistic + Protective → Aggressive + Organized *(although it is historically debatable, he emphasized conquest and administration; meshes with his more forceful Civ IV profile)*; Hatshepsut — Spiritual + Creative → Spiritual + Financial *(historical emphasis on trade/wealth; modest buff in practice)*. Full before/after with rationale in  [Assets Rebalancing table (Leader Traits)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Assets_Rebalancing.md#leaders-traits-rework), or the values and rankings only in the new **Sevopedia Traits' Charts**. *Note: leader "flavors" unchanged.*
 - Barbarian **leader button/icon** is distinct (no longer Genghis Khan’s).

